---
title: Veggie Pizza Squares
servings: 48
cuisine: american
main_protein: dairy
prep_time: "18 minutes"
cook_time: "12 minutes"
tags:
  - appetizer
  - vegetables
image: ../obsidian/attachments/Veggie Pizza Squares.jpeg
prep:
  - Preheat oven to 350°F
  - Lightly grease a 9 x 13 inch pan
  - Finely chop the vegetables
  - Grate the carrot
---

Separate @refrigerator crescent rolls{11.5%oz} and press into lightly greased #9 x 13 inch pan{}, covering bottom to form crust. Bake in 350°F #oven{} for ~{10%minutes} until lightly browned. Cool.

Topping: Mix @spreadable cream cheese{8%oz} (non-fat), @salad dressing{0.5%cup} (low-fat, or mayonnaise) and @ranch dressing mix{1%oz} well in #bowl{}. Spread over cooled crust.

Vegetables: The vegetables given are a guide. You will need a total of about 2 cups (500 mL). Be sure to include some red color for appearance. Mix @celery{2%tbsp}, @red pepper{0.33%cup}, @green pepper{0.33%cup}, @radish{3%tbsp}, @green onion{3%tbsp}, @mushrooms{3%tbsp}, @cauliflower{3%tbsp}, @broccoli{3%tbsp} (all finely chopped) and @carrot{3%tbsp}, grated, well. Sprinkle over topping. Press vegetables into topping. Refrigerate. Cuts into 48 squares.

-- Lots of color, depending on what veggies you choose.
-- Bake the crust the day before. Prepare the topping and vegetables in the morning. Assemble just before serving.
-- 1 square: 33 Calories; 1 g Protein; 1.1 g Total Fat; 5 g Carbohydrate; 121 mg Sodium
